   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">You can use the `summarise_` function when you want to use variables in dplyr functions. Other dplyr functions also have a version with a trailing underscore. For example:<div><br></div><div><div>library(dplyr)</div><div><br></div><div># The usual way of using dplyr</div><div>mtcars %&gt;%</div><div>  group_by(cyl) %&gt;%</div><div>  summarise(meanwt = mean(wt))</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div># Passing in strings in variables</div><div>group &lt;- &quot;cyl&quot;</div><div>var &lt;- &quot;mean(wt)&quot;</div><div>mtcars %&gt;%</div><div>  group_by_(group) %&gt;%</div><div>  summarise_(meanwt = var)</div><div><br></div></div><div>See <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/dplyr/vignettes/nse.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/dplyr/vignettes/nse.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792396817711000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_ZI9Pe6KHyM7GOuzHvJAO\">https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/dplyr/vignettes/nse.html</a> for more information.</div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Sep 9, 2015 at 6:01 AM, msquatrito <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">squa...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
